Title: iM Securities Launches 'iM-Tecton US Stock Lab' Recommending Investments in US Innovation-Led Companies
Body: iM Securities introduced the 'iM-Tecton US Stock Lab' on the 5th, targeting investors who seek continuous alpha returns through US stocks and ETFs. The 'iM-Tecton US Stock Lab' is a discretionary product based on the advisory of Tecton Asset Management. It invests in leading companies in the US with global competitiveness such as AI, semiconductors, and big techs. The portfolio is constructed using large-cap blue-chip stocks with 1 to 2 positions per sector, considering business models and financial structures, and limits individual stock exposure to a maximum of 30% to avoid excessive concentration. iM Securities plans to take proactive portfolio management measures, such as reducing positions based on market conditions if there is an unusual price decline due to the loss of leadership in the management environment of the dominant companies. It also aims to capitalize on exchange rate fluctuations through an open position strategy. An iM Securities official stated, ""The US-led position in the global economy is strengthening, and top-tier companies are being born. The US stock market is leading the global stock market trends."" He explained, ""Building a global portfolio centered around the US is inevitable, and this product will be a useful investment tool for those who wish to invest in US stocks."" The 'iM-Tecton US Stock Lab' requires a minimum investment of 30 million won with a contract period of one year. Contract extension is possible at maturity. Early redemption is allowed, but a redemption fee is charged if done within one year.

